{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function matchesKeyboardEvent(\n   event, \n   hotkey, \n   platform?): boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/match.ts#L49","children":[{"type":"text","value":"match.ts:49"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checks if a KeyboardEvent matches a hotkey."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Physical bindings such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod+[KeyS]"},{"type":"text","value":" match "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.code"},{"type":"text","value":" exactly.\nLogical bindings use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.key"},{"type":"text","value":", with a fallback to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code"},{"type":"text","value":"\nfor letter keys, digit keys (0-9), and punctuation keys when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" produces special\ncharacters (e.g., macOS Option+letter, Shift+number, or Option+punctuation).\nLetter keys are matched case-insensitively."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Also handles \"dead key\" events where "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.key"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'Dead'"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of the expected\ncharacter. This commonly occurs on macOS with Option+letter combinations (e.g., Option+E,\nOption+I, Option+U, Option+N) and on Windows/Linux with international keyboard layouts.\nIn these cases, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.code"},{"type":"text","value":" is used to determine the physical key."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"event","children":[{"type":"text","value":"event"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyboardEvent"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The KeyboardEvent to check"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hotkey","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hotkey"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"| "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/Hotkey.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hotkey"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/ParsedHotkey.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ParsedHotkey"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hotkey string or ParsedHotkey to match against"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"platform","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platform?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"mac\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"windows\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"linux\""}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The target platform for resolving 'Mod' (defaults to auto-detection)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"True if the event matches the hotkey"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"document.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n  if (matchesKeyboardEvent(event, 'Mod+S')) {\n    event.preventDefault()\n    handleSave()\n  }\n})","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"event","text":"event","level":3},{"id":"hotkey","text":"hotkey","level":3},{"id":"platform","text":"platform?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction matchesKeyboardEvent(\n   event, \n   hotkey, \n   platform?): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [match.ts:49](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/match.ts#L49)\n\nChecks if a KeyboardEvent matches a hotkey.\n\nPhysical bindings such as `Mod+[KeyS]` match `event.code` exactly.\nLogical bindings use `event.key`, with a fallback to `code`\nfor letter keys, digit keys (0-9), and punctuation keys when `key` produces special\ncharacters (e.g., macOS Option+letter, Shift+number, or Option+punctuation).\nLetter keys are matched case-insensitively.\n\nAlso handles \"dead key\" events where `event.key` is `'Dead'` instead of the expected\ncharacter. This commonly occurs on macOS with Option+letter combinations (e.g., Option+E,\nOption+I, Option+U, Option+N) and on Windows/Linux with international keyboard layouts.\nIn these cases, `event.code` is used to determine the physical key.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### event\n\n`KeyboardEvent`\n\nThe KeyboardEvent to check\n\n### hotkey\n\n  \\| [`Hotkey`](../type-aliases/Hotkey.md)\n  \\| [`ParsedHotkey`](../type-aliases/ParsedHotkey.md)\n\nThe hotkey string or ParsedHotkey to match against\n\n### platform?\n\n`\"mac\"` \\| `\"windows\"` \\| `\"linux\"`\n\nThe target platform for resolving 'Mod' (defaults to auto-detection)\n\n## Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\nTrue if the event matches the hotkey\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n  if (matchesKeyboardEvent(event, 'Mod+S')) {\n    event.preventDefault()\n    handleSave()\n  }\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: matchesKeyboardEvent\ntitle: matchesKeyboardEvent\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction matchesKeyboardEvent(\n   event, \n   hotkey, \n   platform?): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [match.ts:49](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/match.ts#L49)\n\nChecks if a KeyboardEvent matches a hotkey.\n\nPhysical bindings such as `Mod+[KeyS]` match `event.code` exactly.\nLogical bindings use `event.key`, with a fallback to `code`\nfor letter keys, digit keys (0-9), and punctuation keys when `key` produces special\ncharacters (e.g., macOS Option+letter, Shift+number, or Option+punctuation).\nLetter keys are matched case-insensitively.\n\nAlso handles \"dead key\" events where `event.key` is `'Dead'` instead of the expected\ncharacter. This commonly occurs on macOS with Option+letter combinations (e.g., Option+E,\nOption+I, Option+U, Option+N) and on Windows/Linux with international keyboard layouts.\nIn these cases, `event.code` is used to determine the physical key.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### event\n\n`KeyboardEvent`\n\nThe KeyboardEvent to check\n\n### hotkey\n\n  \\| [`Hotkey`](../type-aliases/Hotkey.md)\n  \\| [`ParsedHotkey`](../type-aliases/ParsedHotkey.md)\n\nThe hotkey string or ParsedHotkey to match against\n\n### platform?\n\n`\"mac\"` \\| `\"windows\"` \\| `\"linux\"`\n\nThe target platform for resolving 'Mod' (defaults to auto-detection)\n\n## Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\nTrue if the event matches the hotkey\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n  if (matchesKeyboardEvent(event, 'Mod+S')) {\n    event.preventDefault()\n    handleSave()\n  }\n})\n```\n"}
